    {
      "version": "module2.2026-08-24.2",
      "reason": "The pre-replay source audit found six multi-offense fixed-drive envelopes. This revision froze the raw-drive and possession-team split, added audit fields, and kept special-teams-only control outside the offensive-series target."
    },
    {
      "version": "module2.2026-08-24.3",
      "reason": "The pre-implementation chronology review replaced a static cross-season calibration holdout with candidate-specific prior prequential residuals. A static fit before a 384-game block would not represent the successive Tuesday information sets inside that block."
    },
    {
      "version": "module2.2026-08-24.4",
      "reason": "The pre-implementation equation audit fixed the league-season baseline's prior strength at 64 games and defined its current-season update exactly."
    },
    {
      "version": "module2.2026-08-24.5",
      "reason": "A second independent pre-score audit blocked v4. This revision freezes the feature dictionary, candidate design, residual boundary, discrete calibration, common-manifest failure rule, bootstrap comparison families, ablation controls, and synthetic fixture assertions. It also separates historical audit ranges from valid count support."
    },
    {
      "version": "module2.2026-08-24.6",
      "reason": "The final pre-score equation audit found that neutral-site games have arbitrary schedule home and away labels. This revision excludes neutral games from P0 home-away location estimation while retaining both teams in P1's pooled league rate."
    },
    {
      "version": "module2.2026-08-24.7",
      "reason": "Two independent pre-replay implementation audits found that the source-missingness threshold, negative-control seeds, shared resample ledger, exact quantile rule, invalid-run path, selection order, and freeze-manifest verification were not fully executable. This revision fixes those contracts before any target-linked candidate score."
    },
    {
      "version": "module2.2026-08-25.8",
      "reason": "The v7 replay terminated protocol_invalid before aggregation or selection. It exposed two target-independent implementation defects: intentional 2010 null indicators were validated before P2 prehistory exclusion, and the runner omitted the already-frozen Tuesday date cutoff for postponed prior-week games. V8 fixes only those execution paths, retains every model, threshold, feature, seed, loss, and gate, and adds boundary tests. No v7 model scorecard, comparison, or gate result was produced or consulted."
    }
